# AwakeTab design rules

Start at `docs/plan/glance/AGENT_PROMPT.md` (the Glance brief; it wins over other docs and over code), then `DESIGN.md` for the design system, `PRODUCT.md` for users, principles and anti-references, and the Glance section of `docs/redesign/DECISIONS.md`. Read the relevant part before editing UI.

- **Pill strings are a contract; never change them:** Ready · Starting… · Screen awake · Paused — tab hidden · Blocked — here's the fix · Tap to use the fallback · Awake via video fallback.
- **Colour roles:** volt green means awake only, violet is the button, amber means paused, red means blocked, sky is focus and information. State is never colour alone.
- **Tokens:** use the tokens in `apps/site/app/globals.css` through their Tailwind names; the extension uses the `--at-*` tokens in `apps/extension/src/styles/tokens.css`. Never hard-code colours, sizes or radii.
- **Themes:** light, dark and OLED, with the system setting followed live.
- **Screen sizes:** design for phone, tablet and desktop.
- **Time:** 12-hour AM/PM for `en`, a full date line, "tomorrow" past midnight, and the end time shown before starting.
- **Motion:** slow and ease-out, with no bounce; everything stops under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- **Markup and CSS:** logical CSS properties only; real buttons and links; targets at least 44 px; inline panels before modals.
- **Copy:** plain, honest, no em dashes in new copy, and no ads on the awake screen.
- **Before any push:** keep all gates green (`pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, `pnpm size`). `main` deploys production.
